Implemented
-----------
- System V shared memory provides `shmget`, `shmat`, `shmdt`, and `shmctl`.
- Shared-memory attachments are inherited by `fork` and cleaned up on `exec` or exit.
- POSIX shared memory supports `shm_open`, `mmap`, and `ftruncate`.
- Shared-memory names use xv6 files and the existing `unlink` syscall.
- `ipcs` lists shared-memory segments and reports their details and limits.
- Separate test programs cover System V and POSIX shared memory.
- `usertests` and `stressfs` tested correctly after adding syscall.

Not Implemented
---------------
- Existing shared-memory mappings are not moved to defragment address space.
- The Linux shared-memory chat demo is not included.
- QEMU does not automatically run the tests, `usertests`, or `stressfs`.
- Other posix syscalls are not implemented yet.
